  "known_limitation_V2": "V2_cash_destination: my simulate_two_asset engine is a strict 2-asset (SPY + one destination leg) engine, so V2 used BIL as the sole non-SPY leg THROUGHOUT (both on- and off-state months). The primary's decide() uses IEF for the off-state in EVERY variant (including V2) and only routes the incremental weight to BIL during on-state months -- i.e. V2 should hold SPY/IEF 60/40 off, SPY/BIL 30/70 on. This is a genuine gap in my V2 implementation (not present for V1/V3/V4, whose destination is IEF -- identical to the off-state leg, so the 2-asset shortcut is exact for them) and explains most of the V2 maxDD/Calmar/A5 mismatch against the primary's V2 numbers. Does not change the overall conclusion: V2 lands in Tier C in both runs either way."
